WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:05.400
Though it made her career, Megan Fox's experiences&nbsp;
filming the first two "Transformers" movies had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:09.240
huge consequences on her professional life and&nbsp;
her relationship with director Michael Bay.

00:00:09.240 --> 00:00:13.320
There's no doubt that Megan Fox is a&nbsp;
talented and beautiful actress. She&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.320 --> 00:00:18.060
was declared the sexiest woman in the world in a&nbsp;
2008 online poll and seemed to be on top of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:22.440
world after she scored the role of Mikaela&nbsp;
Banes in Paramount's "Transformers." Fox,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.440 --> 00:00:25.860
and her co-star Shia LaBeouf, received&nbsp;
major attention for their roles,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.860 --> 00:00:28.980
but there was a moment when the actor's&nbsp;
career took a turn for the worse.

00:00:28.980 --> 00:00:33.060
Hollywood is a fast-paced and ruthless&nbsp;
place, which means that if an actor or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.060 --> 00:00:37.560
actress makes a comment they shouldn't have&nbsp;
or a personal move they might regret, it will,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.560 --> 00:00:41.820
unfortunately, stain their career in some&nbsp;
way or another. For Fox, it all started when&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.820 --> 00:00:45.060
she said something that might have gotten her&nbsp;
"canceled" had it happened a few years later,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.060 --> 00:00:49.080
in the so-called "cancel culture" era.&nbsp;
Of course, everyone makes mistakes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.080 --> 00:00:52.380
and Fox knows that today, but the&nbsp;
toll it took on her is undeniable

00:00:52.380 --> 00:00:57.180
Fox's career didn't start with the "Transformers"&nbsp;
franchise, but it definitely boosted her stardom.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.180 --> 00:01:01.980
It seemed like she was on her way to becoming&nbsp;
an A-lister, until 2009, when she sat down with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.980 --> 00:01:05.640
Wonderland Magazine and talked about her time&nbsp;
on set with "Transformers" director Michael&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.640 --> 00:01:09.540
Bay. When she was asked what it was like to&nbsp;
work with the "Blockbuster King," she said,

00:01:09.540 --> 00:01:12.420
"He's like Napoleon and he&nbsp;
wants to create this insane,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.420 --> 00:01:16.860
infamous madman reputation. He wants to&nbsp;
be like Hitler on his sets, and he is."

00:01:16.860 --> 00:01:20.640
Following her comments, Fox was booted&nbsp;
from the "Transformers" franchise,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:25.620
with her character being written out of 2011's&nbsp;
"Transformers: Dark of the Moon." Fox's fallout&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.620 --> 00:01:30.120
from the billion-dollar series was controversial,&nbsp;
leading to a turbulent case of "he said she said."

00:01:30.120 --> 00:01:35.040
Following the news, Fox's PR team came out&nbsp;
swinging, saying that the actress wasn't fired&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.040 --> 00:01:39.960
from the role, with the decision to quit being all&nbsp;
her own. Shortly after, Michael Bay told GQ that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.960 --> 00:01:44.760
executive producer Steven Spielberg compelled&nbsp;
him to fire Fox for her comments. Shia LaBeouf&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.760 --> 00:01:48.420
added that Fox was let go because she started,&nbsp;
quote, "s--t-talking" the film's "captain."

00:01:48.420 --> 00:01:52.200
Ultimately, Fox and Bay's spat was&nbsp;
short-lived, as they ended up working&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.200 --> 00:01:56.700
together in the live-action reboot of "Teenage&nbsp;
Mutant Ninja Turtles," which Bay produced.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.700 --> 00:02:01.260
Fox never took a break or "quit" acting —&nbsp;
she maintained a constant flow of roles,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.260 --> 00:02:05.160
but it seemed like her career wasn't the same&nbsp;
after her time on "Transformers" was wrapped up.

00:02:05.160 --> 00:02:09.420
It's not a secret that some movie stars&nbsp;
often get typecast into one type of genre.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.420 --> 00:02:13.560
This is unfortunate, of course, and&nbsp;
in the late 2000s, Fox was feeling it.

00:02:13.560 --> 00:02:17.575
"It's weird, I just wouldn't peg&nbsp;
you for mechanical. Oh my god."

00:02:17.575 --> 00:02:19.020
"Oh, you know, I don't really broadcast it."

00:02:19.020 --> 00:02:23.280
In a 2009 interview with Jimmy Kimmel, she&nbsp;
explained how she felt sexualized from the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.280 --> 00:02:27.060
beginning of her career, particularly&nbsp;
in her brief moment in "Bad Boys II."

00:02:27.060 --> 00:02:32.040
Fox also starred in Diablo Cody-penned horror&nbsp;
movie "Jennifer's Body," which gained backlash&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.040 --> 00:02:36.780
due to the sexism that surrounded it. Since then,&nbsp;
the project has become a horror cult classic.

00:02:36.780 --> 00:02:41.940
There's no hidden truth behind Fox being cast&nbsp;
as the "hot girl." In an interview with ET,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.940 --> 00:02:46.260
Cody and Fox reunited and chatted about the&nbsp;
film. Fox revealed that the pressure of being&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.260 --> 00:02:50.700
objectified and oversexualized took a toll on her,&nbsp;
which stemmed from her role in "Transformers."&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.700 --> 00:02:55.380
Since her iteration of the "Teenage Mutant&nbsp;
Ninja Turtles" franchise wrapped up in 2016,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.380 --> 00:02:59.820
Fox hasn't worked with Bay. Her most notable&nbsp;
role since then has been her stint on "New Girl."

00:02:59.820 --> 00:03:03.000
Of course, there's always more to&nbsp;
every story, but her comments about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:06.720
Michael Bay's directing techniques and&nbsp;
major typecasting are just a couple of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.720 --> 00:03:10.380
reasons why Fox was never the same after&nbsp;
her role in the "Transformers" franchise.

